    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d362-a1">

                <pb facs="0536" n="494" xml:id="pg494"/>

                <head>Mr. Welles to Mr.
                        Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Navy Department</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-01-13"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 13, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to enclose herewith copy
                    of a despatch, No. 28, dated the 2d instant, from Acting Rear-Admiral Charles
                    Wilkes, in reply to the complaints presented in the communication addressed to
                    you by Lord Lyons on the 24th November, and which you referred to when you
                    transmitted to me a copy of your note to Lord Lyons on the 5th ultimo.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>GIDEON WELLES, <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of the
                        Navy.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
